{%- comment -%}
  Extension point provided by al_folio_core's _layouts/bib.liquid:

      {% capture hook_exists %}{% file_exists _includes/hook/bib.liquid %}{% endcapture %}
      {% if hook_exists == 'true' %}{% include hook/bib.liquid %}{% endif %}

  It runs once per bibliography entry, with `entry` in scope, and whatever it outputs is
  placed just above the journal/date line. Using the hook rather than overriding the
  411-line theme layout means theme upgrades keep working.

  Why this exists: two facts in the bibliography carry real academic weight and were
  rendering as ordinary grey text, indistinguishable from a journal name —

    * co-first authorship (`authorship = {co-first}`, 5 entries) — this feeds directly
      into how a publication record is assessed; burying it costs the author.
    * preprint status (`keywords = {preprint}`, 1 entry) — the opposite problem: a
      non-peer-reviewed item must never read as a journal publication on a public page.

  Both are semantic values set in the bibliography source of truth, deliberately kept out
  of the free-text `note` field so that no renderer has to string-match prose that might
  later be reworded. This file only decides how they look; the source decides what is
  true. Colours come from al-folio's theme custom properties, so the badges follow
  light/dark mode without any extra stylesheet.

  `authorship` is listed in `filtered_bibtex_keywords` in _config.yml, which stops the
  theme from also dumping it as a raw field on the page.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign flag_style = "display:inline-block;margin:0 0 0.25rem 0;padding:0.1rem 0.5rem;border-radius:0.2rem;font-size:0.75rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0.02em;line-height:1.5;" -%}

{%- if entry.keywords contains "preprint" -%}
  <span
    style="{{ flag_style }}color:var(--global-warning-block-title);border:1px solid var(--global-warning-block);background:var(--global-warning-block-bg);"
    title="Not peer reviewed. This is a preprint, not a journal publication."
    >Preprint &middot; not peer reviewed</span
  >
{%- endif -%}

{%- if entry.authorship contains "co-first" -%}
  <span
    style="{{ flag_style }}color:var(--global-theme-color);border:1px solid var(--global-theme-color);background:transparent;"
    title="Shared first authorship on this paper."
    >Co-first author</span
  >
{%- endif -%}
